            <ArticleTitle>Hypoglycemia after gastric bypass: An emerging complication.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>319-328</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3949/ccjm.84a.16064</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As the obesity epidemic worsens, more people are opting for weight-loss surgery, including gastric bypass. Of the possible complications associated with this procedure, hypoglycemia secondary to hyperinsulinemia is becoming a more common and therefore more relevant problem.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017 Cleveland Clinic.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
